After each instruction the symbolic stack, read from bottom to top, names the values that the portable machine would hold in that order. At block entry the incoming edge establishes the invariant for every slot. The method may keep parameters for values a downstream pass can prove dead or identical on all edges; the extra work for lowering transfers is proportional to the sum of stack heights passed along those edges.
